# UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suppressions for the Sanitizer Tests workflow
# (.github/workflows/sanitizers.yml loads this file through UBSAN_OPTIONS).
#
# Only defects inside third-party or ecosystem code belong here, each with the
# upstream issue and the condition for removing it. Never suppress
# pacs_system code: a pacs_system test that fails under a sanitizer is
# quarantined in ctest-quarantine-<sanitizer>.txt with its issue instead.
# A pattern matches the source file of the report as a substring.

# OpenJPH allocator alignment suppressions were removed with the 0.30.1 pin
# (#1288), after all 15 HTJ2K cases passed with the codec and OpenJPH compiled
# with -fsanitize=alignment and no suppression file on arm64. This includes
# allocator fix OpenJPH#262 and generic decoder memcpy loads from OpenJPH#291.

# OpenJPH 0.30.1 generic RCT (32- and 64-bit transformed lines) left-shifts
# negative green samples, which is undefined before C++20:
# https://github.com/aous72/OpenJPH/issues/406
# Fixed upstream by PR405, commit c7a4d43942d2f92fdc385a8c4148a9b523063192,
# but no published release includes that fix as checked on 2026-11-01.
# Only a C++14 OpenJPH needs this entry (its default and the vcpkg port's mode).
# A FetchContent build inherits C++20, where the shift is defined and reports
# nothing, so the htj2k-arm64-ubsan job runs that mode with no suppression file.
# Its C++14 mode keeps unsuppressed reproducers and an unrelated shift control.
# Remove this entry and the expected-failure probes when a fixed release is
# adopted. This is tracked suppressed coverage, not a fix (#1299).
shift-base:openjph-src/src/core/transform/ojph_colour.cpp
